00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:25.080
In 1907, the American economy experienced a great state of

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:28.400
panic and financial awe that galvanized people to banks

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:34.800
to withdraw their deposits. The main reason that ignited the crisis was a failed attempt by a group of speculators

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:39.290
to acquire shares of the United Copper Company in order to manipulate prices.

00:00:39.290 --> 00:00:44.360
At that time, the United States was the main financial power Who did not have a central bank.

00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:48.360
However, After the severe economic turmoil caused by this financial chaos,

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:52.880
such as the inability of banks to return depositors' money and the bankruptcy of many American companies;

00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:58.840
There were calls for the need to establish a financial institution to prevent such panic and turmoil.

00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:03.708
Then, 6 years later, specifically on December 23, 1913,

00:01:03.708 --> 00:01:07.596
US President Woodrow Wilson signed the Federal Reserve Act

00:01:07.596 --> 00:01:12.440
to establish the Federal Reserve or the American Central Bank.

00:01:12.440 --> 00:01:21.840
Over time, the US Federal Reserve, 109 years old, became the most dangerous and influential financial institution in the whole world.

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:25.099
The role of the Federal Reserve is to achieve two main goals,

00:01:25.099 --> 00:01:29.080
which are often referred to as the Dual Mandate.

00:01:29.080 --> 00:01:34.000
The first goal is to direct the US economy towards maximum sustainable employment.

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:39.640
The second goal: is to maintain price stability or control inflation levels

00:01:39.640 --> 00:01:48.000
any economy has a specific imposed speed just like the speed of the car, so that it does not run persistently above or below its imposed rate 

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:53.520
Otherwise, there will be many economic problems such as inflation, deflation, unemployment...etc.

00:01:53.520 --> 00:02:00.360
When the American economy grows too quickly or too slowly,

00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:03.840
the US Federal Reserve intervenes to adjust the speed through the monetary policy

00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:06.080
that it is responsible for managing it economically.

00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:09.920
One of the courses that can carry out this task is interest rates.

00:02:09.920 --> 00:02:13.860
Although they are all internal decisions concerning the American economy,

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:20.840
their impact transcends American borders and goes beyond the United States to all global markets,

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:26.760
and affects the living standards of individuals in developing and emerging countries specifically like the economies of Arab countries.

00:02:26.760 --> 00:02:33.160
That is why it is necessary for us as Arabs to understand the impact of the Federal Reserve’s decisions and their long term consequences.

00:02:33.160 --> 00:02:40.320
The global influence of the American Federal Reserve is of course due to the fact that the American economy is the largest in the world.

00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:44.400
The American dollar is the dominant currency in the global economy.

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:50.080
We have even seen over the course of the previous six weeks the power of the cosmopolitan American economics

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:53.520
over the Russian economy after the Russian war on Ukraine.

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:59.320
As known, the US Federal Reserve raised interest rates on Wednesday, March 16th.

00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:04.400
Here a main question arises: What is the impact of such a dangerous decision on the Arab countries?

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:11.840
Moreover, we need to know why the Fed raised the interest rate, and what is this institution’s function in the American economy?

